---
code: K0013
title: Toplevel Expression
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, top-level, expression, declaration]
description: "Bare expression is not allowed at the top level of a file"
---

The top level of a Kura source file only permits declarations and top-level rules—specifically `let` bindings (and redefinitions), `type` declarations, `fn` definitions, `test` blocks, `extern` declarations, `use` imports, `set` rules, and `static-assert` statements. Bare expressions (such as function calls, UI elements, arithmetic, or control-flow blocks) cannot appear directly at the top level.

## Example

This error occurs when an expression or UI element is placed directly at the root of a file instead of inside a function, binding, or `test` block:

```kura
#text("Hello, world!")

compute(10, 20)

if ready {
  start()
} else {
  stop()
}
```

## Solution

Wrap the expression in a `fn` declaration (such as a view or helper function), bind its result with `let`, or place it inside a `test` block:

```kura
fn main() => #text("Hello, world!")

let result = compute(10, 20)

test "startup check" {
  let state = if ready { start() } else { stop() }
  assert(state == true)
}
```
